    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0317" n="1051" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1051"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Hicks.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 227.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received Mr. Neill’s dispatch No.
                    411, of the 3d ultimo, in regard to the claim of the Hydrographic Commission of
                    the Amazon.</p>
                <p>Now that the Peruvian Congress is again in session, the Department hopes to
                    secure intelligence that this admittedly just and long-standing claim may be
                    satisfactorily disposed of.</p>
                <p>You will accordingly continue your efforts to that end.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
